---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { getRawImage } from "../../lib/images";
import { getClient } from "../../lib/manifest";

const client = getClient("ps")!;
const cover = getRawImage("ps", "PS1")!;
const shots = ["PS7", "PS8", "PS9", "PS10", "PS12"]
  .map((label) => ({ label, img: getRawImage("ps", label) }))
  .filter((s) => s.img);
---
<Base title="Powered Storage — Zoltán Kosa-Szántó" description="On demand storage, RV power and work containers, North Carolina. Brand and site work that taught the market a category it didn't have a name for yet.">
  <section class="section wrap case-hero">
    <div class="hero-frame">
      <Image src={cover} alt="Powered Storage brand and site work" widths={[600, 1000, 1600]} sizes="(min-width: 860px) 1280px, 100vw" priority />
    </div>
    <div class="case-meta">
      <div>
        <h1>Powered Storage</h1>
        <p class="dek">They had an empty lot and no name for what they were renting out.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="label tags">Brand Identity &middot; Digital Platform &middot; GTM</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap case-body">
    <p class="eyebrow">On demand storage, RV power and work containers &middot; North Carolina</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        On demand storage. RV power pedestals. Work containers for tradesmen. Flex space,
        secured and climate controlled. None of it fit a category people already searched for.
        The offer wasn't the problem. Nobody knew to look for it yet, so the brand and the site
        had to teach the market the category existed before anyone could sell into it.
      </p>

      <p>
        The work covers identity, the investor and brand materials, ad graphics for the
        individual services (RV power, work containers, flex space), and the website. Different
        audiences, one system: a tradesman looking for a place to park a container and an
        investor looking at the same company both had to read it clearly.
      </p>

      <p class="outcome">Filled the yard. Retained tenants. Built the local reputation from zero.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shots">
    <div class="wrap grid">
      {shots.map(({ label, img }) => (
        <Image src={img!} alt={`Powered Storage, ${label}`} widths={[400, 700, 1000]} sizes="(min-width: 860px) 50vw, 100vw" loading="lazy" />
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap next">
    <a class="link-arrow" href="/work/">&larr; Back to work</a>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-hero { padding-block-end: 0; }
  .hero-frame { background: var(--surface-subtle); }
  .hero-frame :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .case-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: start;
    gap: 24px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding-block-start: 32px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin-block-start: 32px;
  }
  .case-meta h1 { font-weight: 300; font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px); }
  .dek {
    max-width: 46ch;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 18px;
    margin-block-start: 12px;
  }
  .tags { white-space: nowrap; padding-block-start: 6px; }

  .case-body { padding-block-start: 0; }
  .case-body .eyebrow { margin-block-end: 28px; display: block; }
  .case-body p:not(.eyebrow) { margin-block-end: 20px; color: var(--ink); }
  .outcome {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .shots {
    background: var(--gallery-ground);
    padding-block: var(--space-section-mobile);
  }
  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .shots { padding-block: var(--space-section-desktop); }
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  .grid :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 2px; }
  .next { padding-block-start: 56px; }
</style>
